# RAG System Guidelines

## Code Context First

Before editing any file, always retrieve code context via the RAG repo-agent:

```bash
uv run rag repo-agent --repo <repo-name> --json "<task>"
```

Parse the JSON evidence bundle before opening files:
- `evidence_bundle.top_files` — most relevant files
- `evidence_bundle.symbols` — extracted symbol names
- `evidence_bundle.callers` — call tree data
- `evidence_bundle.tests` — related test files
- `evidence_bundle.modules` — module boundaries
- `evidence_bundle.docs` — project knowledge (events, DI maps)
- `resolve.usages` vs `resolve.usages_raw` — filtered vs total blast radius

## Repo Names

- Signal-Android: `signal` (not `signal-android`)

## Narrow Lookups

For specific symbol lookups, use graph tools directly:

```bash
uv run rag node <SymbolName> --repo <repo-name> --json
uv run rag callers <SymbolName> --repo <repo-name> --json
uv run rag impact <SymbolName> --repo <repo-name> --json
```

## Config

- Default config: `config/default.toml`
- User config: `~/.rag/config.toml`
- Retrieval LLM is configurable via `[retrieval_agent]` section (gemini, openai, anthropic, ollama)
